        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d3aad9a1-1ab7-593e-822e-08e46aa447ab",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Catherine O'Hara, Charlie Tahan, Winona Ryder, Martin Short, Tim Burton, Christopher Guest\n- Films: Frankenweenie, Beetlejuice, Edward Scissorhands, The Nightmare Before Christmas, Mars Attacks!, After Hours, Home Alone, Waiting for Guffman, Best in Show, A Mighty Wind, For Your Consideration\n- Television: Second City Television, Ozark\n- Roles: Victor Frankenstein\n\nFacts:\n- Catherine Anne O'Hara was born on March 4, 1954, and she is a Canadian-American actress, writer, and comedian.\n- Catherine O'Hara was known for comedy work on Second City Television from 1976 to 1984.\n- Catherine O'Hara appeared in the film After Hours in 1985.\n- Catherine O'Hara appeared in the film Beetlejuice in 1988.\n- Catherine O'Hara appeared in the film Home Alone in 1990.\n- Catherine O'Hara appeared in the film The Nightmare Before Christmas in 1993.\n- Catherine O'Hara appeared in Christopher Guest's mockumentary films Waiting for Guffman in 1996, Best in Show in 2000, A Mighty Wind in 2003, and For Your Consideration in 2006.\n- Charles \"Charlie\" Tahan was born on June 11, 1998, and he is an American actor.\n- Charlie Tahan voiced Victor Frankenstein in the animated film Frankenweenie.\n- Charlie Tahan is known for playing Wyatt on Ozark.\n- The 2012 film Frankenweenie had voice cast members Winona Ryder, Catherine O'Hara, and Martin Short, who had all worked with Tim Burton on previous films.\n- Winona Ryder had previously worked with Tim Burton on Beetlejuice and Edward Scissorhands, Catherine O'Hara had previously worked with Tim Burton on Beetlejuice and The Nightmare Before Christmas, and Martin Short had previously worked with Tim Burton on Mars Attacks!.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6e8ac416-d6e5-5be0-953a-b0e558ec889c",
        "text": "Page: Frankenweenie (2012 film). Sentence: The voice cast includes four actors who worked with Burton on previous films: Winona Ryder (\"Beetlejuice\" and \"Edward Scissorhands\"); Catherine O'Hara (\"Beetlejuice\" and \"The Nightmare Before Christmas\"); Martin Short (\"Mars Attacks!\nPage: Catherine O'Hara. Sentence: Catherine Anne O'Hara {'1': \", '2': \", '3': \", '4': \"} (born March 4, 1954) is a Canadian-American actress, writer, and comedian.\nPage: Catherine O'Hara. Sentence: She is known for her comedy work on \"Second City Television\" (1976–84) and in films such as \"After Hours\" (1985), \"Beetlejuice\" (1988), \"Home Alone\" (1990), \"\" (1992), and \"The Nightmare Before Christmas\" (1993).\nPage: Catherine O'Hara. Sentence: Her other film appearances include the mockumentary films written and directed by Christopher Guest: \"Waiting for Guffman\" (1996), \"Best in Show\" (2000), \"A Mighty Wind\" (2003), and \"For Your Consideration\" (2006).\nPage: Charlie Tahan. Sentence: Charles \"Charlie\" Tahan (born June 11, 1998) is an American actor known for playing \"Wyatt\" on Ozark and for voicing Victor Frankenstein in the animated movie Frankenweenie.",
